"""Detect a separately tokenized s, especially %s and optional plurals.

A percent sign before a lowercase s gives the strongest negative response.
An attached '(s' after a word-sized chunk resembles an optional plural.
Other s tokens are weaker; case, separating punctuation and the preceding
chunk's length distinguish suffixes, acronyms and numeric uses. This
captures the common forms, not the component's word-specific variation.
Message boundaries and opening/closing tool or thought blocks have small
additional responses; chat-start and text-end markers are positive when
they are the first token in a document.
