Predict a positive end-of-text marker and negative punctuation/backslash
combinations, with larger responses for braces, quotes, and compound delimiters.
Chinese numeral 一 ('one') is negative, especially when it ends an unfinished
quantifier phrase. It is much weaker inside completed words. Mathematical
subscript/superscript braces also receive a small negative response.
These token-shape rules omit smaller lexical and context-specific variation.
