"""Layer-0 MLP neuron 5075 (down_proj): an "old vs new" word detector.

It fires on words that say how old or new a thing is, relative to now:
- "old", "former" (and 旧/舊 and other old-word translations): strongest, about 2.5 to 3.5;
- "new", "existing" (and new-word translations): about 1.4;
- "previous", "previously", "retired", "deprecated", "original", "older", "veteran",
  (and 陈/老/以前): about 1.0;
- "now", "present", "once", "past": about 0.6.
It is a lookup on the newest token. An age ("3 years old") is weak, not "former".
No state is carried between positions. Each word has one value, so it ignores context
beyond that age rule.
