Defaults and returns give the strongest English responses. Inflections,
code identifiers, and several translations also respond. Whitespace, case,
and a little grammatical context adjust their strength: declarations and
indentation raise get/return, while pronouns lower get. Most compounds are
weaker than the root alone; getDefault is strong. Other tokens stay near zero.
Only the previous token is remembered, resetting at document boundaries.
