"""A spelling-and-formatting approximation, not a universal phonetic rule.

Short si-like fragments produce negative activations, strongest for 'si'
itself and vowel-plus-si endings. Related syllables in other scripts also
respond. Most longer words are near zero. Separately, tab-separated columns
respond more negatively than continued indentation. Only the preceding token
is remembered; that memory is reset between documents.
