"""Approximate a pulse on line-initial numbers and structural markers.

Training examples fire especially on digits and list signs immediately after a
newline, not on ordinary words. The rules below reproduce that contrast.

A token immediately after a newline gets a content-dependent pulse: strongest
for digits and list signs, smaller for quotation, brackets and single letters.
